      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is actually causing an issue with pens: The pen systems widely used across many worlds allow desktop users to hold down the Tab key to lock the drawing plane, which is essential for writing legible text and drawing clean illustrations. However, when a player is in front of me, that player is automatically selected instead, preventing me from drawing.\n\nja:\n\n実際に悪影響は出ていて、例えばワールドに設置されているペン（QvPenやUniStylusなど）には、Tabキーを押し続けることで平面上に描くことができる機能があります。この機能は可読性の高い文字や絵を描くために必要ですが、プレイヤーが目の前にいるとき、そのプレイヤーの選択が優先されて描けなくなります。",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-09-18T15:51:46.305Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, when the cursor lands on a user using the Tab key, that user is automatically selected. However, in desktop mode, the primary use cases for the Tab key are typically interacting with world-space UI elements or selecting pickup objects. As a result, unintentionally selecting users while navigating with the Tab key can negatively impact the user experience.",
